    "lead": "Soaring to 6,189 meters (20,305 feet) in the heart of the Khumbu Valley, Island Peak (Imja Tse) is Nepal's most coveted trekking peak. While attempted in both spring and autumn, the Spring climbing season (March to May) offers a magical combination of warming alpine temperatures, longer daylight hours, stable headwall snow conditions, and shared summit energy with Everest expeditions. Curated by our veteran IFMGA/NNMGA-certified Sherpa climbing leaders at Igloo Himalaya Treks, here is the complete insider guide to climbing Island Peak in Spring.",
